g chopsticks and eating from a  bowl the decision to stop publication  and licensing of this and five other  books was made after months of  discussion  the company says it's committed to  representing and supporting all  communities and families  books by dr seuss have been translated  into multiple languages  as well as into braille and are sold in  more than 100 countries  no more masks no more restrictions  coming up the american states getting  rid  of pandemic protocols  the biden administration signaling a  tougher stance against russia has  announced new sanctions targeting senior  russian officials  over the poisoning of opposition leader  alexei navalny  the sanctions target seven top business  and political figures including russia's  top spy  and 14 entities involved in the  production of chemical and biological  agents  the sanctions prevent the top figures  allied with russian president vladimir  putin from accessing financial and  property assets in the u.s  these are the first sanctions against  russia by the biden administration  russia is threatening to retaliate the  valley is serving a two and a half year  sentence at one of russia's  harshest prison camps today president  biden announced the u.s  expects it will have enough coronavirus  vaccine doses for every adult american  by the end of may and two u.s states are  now taking major steps toward reopening  the governors of texas and mississippi  have announced they are ending their  statewide mass  mandates they are also allowing  businesses to return to full capacity  yesterday texas recorded more than eight  thousand new covid19 cases  family tragedy ahead what happens when  the front line hits home for healthcare  workers  frontline healthcare workers dealing  with covid patients not only worry about  getting sick themselves but  about bringing the virus home they take  extra precautions to minimize the risk  of course but  that is not foolproof karen lieberman  has one woman's heartbreaking story  hi i'm anisa the safety officer safety  specialists work behind the scenes  they support frontline healthcare staff  ensuring they have adequate supplies and  personal protective  equipment you have all the tools that  you guys need and that they're following  safety protocols  we understand a stressful time at the  end of the day want to be safe and go  home to our family safely  for anissa khan until recently that  included distance visits with her  parents  here i am pushing staff at work to be  safe  not to get it and whatever and lo and  behold  my family end up getting it first it was  khan who tested positive for covid19  then her mother then her father fell ill  too  when i went to go visit him he was i  guess  rodney bergeau was rushed to hospital in  early december  he's been there ever since he had a  condition that we call ards or acute  respiratory distress syndrome he had  a really profound needs for oxygen  both parents critically ill one  wouldn't make it it was very difficult  and then the next morning we get the  phone call from the icu physician saying  you know what we have to integrate your  debt burja was unaware his wife marilyn  had passed  more than two weeks later on his 70th  birthday  he needed a tracheotomy losing mom and  then  hanging on desperately that dad won't be  another one gone  fortunately he began improving and dad's  up in the chair looking like a million  dollars  every day khan facetimes her father to  check in  or visit him in person he was starting  to ask about mom how she doing where is  she  the family had to share the  heartbreaking news his wife  did not survive but he is on the road to  recovery  and with the tube removed from his neck  he has his voice back  rodney how are you feeling oh not too  bad  i take it one day at a time for khan  seeing her own family struggle  has been hard i never thought i'd be  here in a million years  and here i am and a reminder to others  instead of snap a finger things can  change very  very quickly for you karen lieberman  global news  toronto  trying to wrangle up support next the  sports debate in alberta  it is a cliche to think alberta is all  about cowboys ranches and oil fields but  there is a push right now to elevate the  status of rodeos to make them  alberta's official sport heather yurix  west explains why  some believe the sport deserves a leg up  nanton alberta's logan bird is a  canadian champion in tie  down roping but right now he can only  compete  in the united states for me at the  professional level  there was nothing since covet hit there  hasn't been one event  every member of the bird family is  heavily involved in rodeo  it's how they make their living so it's  no surprise they fully support  efforts to make rodeo alberta's official  sport  it absolutely should be an official  sport there's lots of people and  i mean a lot that make their living with  rodeo the private member's bill was put  forward by a calgary united conservative  party mla  who was introduced to rodeo culture  later in life  the significance of of this event in  rural  alberta it just was just it was just  amazing it brought people together  muhammad yasin grew up in pakistan but  fell in love with rodeo after coming to  alberta as  a young man designating rodeo as an  official sport would be a mainly  symbolic gesture but it isn't being  welcomed  by everyone rodeo is frankly a very  risky sport that causes intense amounts  of suffering and regularly causes death  alberta shouldn't be considering  celebrating rodeo as the provincial  sport it should be considering banning  this activity  the province has not yet decided when  rodeo events in alberta might be able to  resume  the birds hope it happens soon the  ability to come  home and get back to work more important  than any gesture of goodwill  heather your ex-west global news calgary  and that is global national for this  tuesday i'm donna friesen  we leave you tonight with a bit of news  from music legend dolly parton  she got a dose of her own medicine today  dolly donated 1 million dollars to help  develop the moderna vaccine and  she encouraged others today by changing  the lyrics of one of her songs  vaccine vaccine vaccine vaccine  i'm begging of you please don't hesitate  to anyone feeling a little fearful dolly  says don't be  such a chicken squat her words not mine  thanks for watching hope to see you here  again tomorrow  take care of yourselves bye-bye
 

